&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the smart buildings design and implementation of automated test scripts and standardized workflows for EV charging features, from initial development through utility energization and final customer activation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary technical lead ensuring seamless integration between vehicle mechatronic embedded controls, charging hardware, and cloud-based mobile applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and enforce rigorous quality standards and testing strategies, integrating automated test suites into CI/CD pipelines to ensure continuous delivery of high-quality charging infrastructure.Define and enforce rigorous quality standards and testing strategies, integrating automated test suites into CI/CD pipelines to ensure continuous delivery of high-quality charging infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify process inefficiencies and lead implementation of automation virtualization opportunities to reduce manual testing and streamline commissioning activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product managers, developers, and feature owners while managing external commissioning vendors to ensure all site technical requirements are met.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adhere to and enforce all safety precautions, particularly regarding high-voltage systems and on-vehicle testing, treating safety as the top priority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide others in best practices, frameworks, and troubleshooting methodologies for complex electrification systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A Bachelor’s degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Business, or a related technical field.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;5+ years of relevant experience with automation/scripting, specifically with high proficiency in Python and experience with frameworks like Autobot or similar.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive technical experience with electrification features, EV charging infrastructure deployment, and the commissioning lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of CI/CD pipelines and tools such as GitHub, Jenkins, or Azure DevOps, along with version control systems like Git.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead cross-functional teams and manage complex projects that involve both hardware-in-the-loop (HIL) bench work and in-vehicle testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to communicate technical issues, project status, and strategic recommendations to leadership and external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Master’s degree or PhD in Engineering or a Master’s in Business Administration (MBA).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of test automation experience with a focus on web/mobile applications and vehicle-to-grid integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with automotive diagnostic tools such as INCA, MDA, CANalyzer, or Vehicle Spy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of Vehicle Electrical Architecture (e.g., VIP, SDV) and serial data buses including LIN, CAN, GMLAN, and Ethernet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High voltage or electrified vehicle safety training and hands-on experience with on-vehicle serial protocols.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certification in Quality Assurance and/or Test Automation (e.g., Six Sigma, ISTQB) and experience with JIRA/Problem Resolution Tracking Systems (PRTS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
