&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;As part of Waymo&#39;s Legal team, you will work on the exciting legal issues surrounding our transformational autonomous driving technology and help drive our business lines forward from technology ideation through scaled commercial deployment. We partner with our public policy, safety, security and privacy experts to define transportation policy for the autonomous driving world to come, advising on regulatory changes that support and protect our users around the world. We collaborate with our engineering, product, strategy and operations teams to develop and protect our intellectual property portfolio and drive our corporate and commercial transactions. We ensure compliance with an increasingly complex and dynamic range of global regulations. And we anticipate, mitigate, and litigate high-profile and precedent-setting legal matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;In this hybrid role, you will report to the Head of Insurance Infrastructure&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the collection, compilation, and validation of underwriting data for insurance renewals across all lines of business. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage Certificate of Insurance (COI) requests and review incoming vendor/contractor COIs to ensure compliance with Waymo&#39;s risk management standards. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review insurance binders, endorsements, policy documentation, and premium invoicing to verify precision against negotiated program terms and retentions. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with internal teams (Legal, Compliance, Operations) as the point of contact for routine insurance inquiries and requirements. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate day-to-day processes with external partners, including insurance brokers, insurers, and other parties. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional attention to detail, strong organizational skills, and a thorough approach towards operational deliverables. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive, solution-oriented mindset and the ability to independently manage competing priorities with tight deadlines &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to articulate insurance requirements and collaborate effectively across diverse internal and external partners. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial insurance operations experience within a corporate risk management department, commercial insurance brokerage, or underwriting organization. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical and quantitative aptitude, comfortable navigating spreadsheets and AI tools to analyze Waymo&#39;s insurance and risk management programs. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working within innovative, fast-paced technology, and dynamic environments. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of contractual risk transfer, indemnity clauses, and insurance compliance monitoring. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional insurance certifications or progress toward designations (e.g., ARM, CPCU, CRIS, or equivalent). &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Risk Management, Finance, Business Administration, Economics, or a related field. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The expected base salary range for this full-time position across US locations is listed below. Actual starting pay will be based on job-related factors, including exact work location, experience, relevant training and education, and skill level. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for the role location or, if the role can be performed remote, the specific salary range for your preferred location, during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Waymo employees are also eligible to participate in Waymo’s discretionary annual bonus program, equity incentive plan, and generous Company benefits program, subject to eligibility requirements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$125,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$152,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;On the Waymo Marketing team, you will help to connect people with the magic and impact of Waymo&#39;s autonomous driving technology. Our team has the unique opportunity to not only grow Waymo&#39;s brand from the ground up, but to also build societal acceptance for autonomous driving technology for the first time in history. We build thoughtful marketing strategy, positioning, messaging and creative assets to deliver messages that matter to our audience, communicated through anything from video content, to social media interactions, to immersive physical experiences. We also shape Waymo&#39;s go-to-market initiatives, helping to transform Waymo into a thriving business with a growing user base.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this hybrid role, you will report to a Group Creative Marketing Lead.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pioneer International Brand Creative: &lt;/strong&gt;Partnering with local marketing agencies to translate Waymo’s frontier autonomous driving technology into clear, emotionally resonant, and human-centered campaigns across international markets. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct &amp;amp; Embed with Agency Partners:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with world-class international creative agencies, embedding with local teams to co-create campaigns that preserve core brand tenets while unlocking deep cultural resonance. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Govern Brand Guidelines &amp;amp; Standards:&lt;/strong&gt; Own visual identity guidelines and verbal brand voice across international channels, providing oversight to prevent brand drift and ensure cross-market consistency. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Translate Business Briefs into Creative Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Translate complex business objectives and localized audience insights into clear, actionable and compelling briefs for creative teams. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architect Repeatable Creative Systems:&lt;/strong&gt; Architect and optimize modular creative templates and AI-assisted workflows to enable partner agencies to deliver localized creative assets at speed without sacrificing craft. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Elite Creative Pedigree:&lt;/strong&gt; 10+ years of experience in copywriting, brand creative, or creative direction, backed by an exceptional portfolio demonstrating both verbal and visual craftsmanship. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;International Localization Expertise:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Deep experience creating TV, digital, and experiential campaigns for diverse international audiences and regional consumer behaviors. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agency &amp;amp; Vendor Direction Mastery:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven track record of managing and directing top-tier global agencies and production partners to drive creative excellence under aggressive timelines. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full-Funnel Campaign Track Record:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven ability to scale creative from massive brand initiatives down to always-on paid social and performance conversion stages. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tech Storytelling Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; Exceptional ability to translate sophisticated emerging technologies into clear, simple, and emotionally resonant consumer messaging. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;International Brand Scaling: &lt;/strong&gt;Experience expanding and scaling a consumer brand internationally, adapting large-scale marketing campaigns to respect local cultural nuances while maintaining cohesive global standards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance Creative Mindset:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;A proven track record of using creative performance metrics and rapid testing to optimize campaign copy and conversion. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive &amp;amp; Stakeholder Management:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Masterful stakeholder management skills, with a track record of pitching bold creative directions and resolving conflicting stakeholder visions. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-Multiplier Fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; Advanced fluency with Generative AI and AI-assisted creative tools, utilizing emerging technologies as a strategic multiplier to accelerate creative ideation and production. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Frontier Tech Focus:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Direct experience or a passionate curiosity for translating autonomous vehicles, robotics, or frontier technologies into understandable and compelling consumer-facing stories. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Experience collaborating closely with non-marketing partners, including Product, Engineering, and Public Affairs, to align creative work with technical milestones and safety narratives. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The expected base salary range for this full-time position across US locations is listed below. Actual starting pay will be based on job-related factors, including exact work location, experience, relevant training and education, and skill level. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for the role location or, if the role can be performed remote, the specific salary range for your preferred location, during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Waymo employees are also eligible to participate in Waymo’s discretionary annual bonus program, equity incentive plan, and generous Company benefits program, subject to eligibility requirements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$210,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$259,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;The Waymo Safety team works to promote and help to continuously improve the safety of Waymo’s fully autonomous driving technology. Our experts develop safety goals and strategies, and conduct safety engineering analyses to ensure safety is being considered throughout the design and development of our vehicles. The team develops and promotes safety strategies and policies for autonomous vehicles for its work with regulatory authorities, lawmakers, law enforcement and public and non-profit organizations. Our Safety Team also helps advise on compliance with applicable environmental, health, and safety regulations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this hybrid role, you will report to the Head of Safety Management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set Standardization Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop a thoughtful, coordinated, company-wide strategy and approach for Waymo’s engagement with SDOs (inclusive of ISO, IEEE, SAE), defining clear goals, levels of engagement, and governance processes for content accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Act as an Internal/External Medium:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as the primary liaison between Waymo&#39;s internal practices and external Standard Development Organizations, actively working to consolidate internal consensus and assess how Waymo’s practices align with or differentiate from external ones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run Internal Training:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and run internal training programs to align engineering, product, and cross-functional teams on external standardization landscapes, compliance goals, and Waymo’s internal stances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape Industry Optionality:&lt;/strong&gt; Strategically prioritize Waymo&#39;s participation in working groups to contribute to shape consensus and advance safety across space while retaining the necessary optionality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Publication and Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead efforts to formulate and publish Waymo&#39;s internal best. practices to external committees, continuing to establish Waymo as a critical partner across the industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Coordination:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate closely with the rest of the Safety Management and Best Practices (SMBP) team, legal regulatory groups, and engineering to establish appropriate platforms for critiquing perspectives and consolidating a consistent positioning on topics of interest.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 7+ years of experience actively engaging with and participating in Standards Development Organizations (e.g., ISO, IEEE, SAE), inclusive of ISO TC 22 SC 32/36/39; ISO TC 204; SAE ORAD.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of developing and setting corporate strategy for standardization engagement within a highly technical or safety-critical domain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build consensus, translate complex external requirements into actionable internal policies, and serve as a medium between technical teams and external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of automotive safety frameworks, Verification &amp;amp; Validation methods, and behavioral evaluation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication skills with the ability to represent the company publicly, navigate ambiguity, and maintain poise in committee settings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior leadership positions or placements on umbrella committees within ISO, SAE, or IEEE that allow visibility into multiple subcommittees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and running internal training programs or educational initiatives across complex matrix organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of contributions to published scholarly literature, recommended practices, or technical reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Waymo’s approach to safety and its safety case&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel requirements&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel is required for key SDO committee meetings, conferences, and team onsites.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The expected base salary range for this full-time position is listed below. Actual starting pay will be based on job-related factors, including exact work location, experience, relevant training and education, and skill level.&amp;nbsp; Waymo employees are also eligible to participate in Waymo’s discretionary annual bonus program, equity incentive plan, and generous Company benefits program, subject to eligibility requirements. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;£141,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;£148,000 GBP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo Operations は、Waymo Driver を世界に届けるための存在です。私たちは、世界初となる大型の自動運転フリートおよびオペレーション プラットフォームを構築し、スケーリングするグローバル チームです。部品調達から&lt;br&gt;エンド カスタマーの管理まで、Waymo Driver を大規模かつ組織的に展開することで Waymo の価値を実現・創造します。Waymo は、協働と称賛を促す文化の構築に尽力しています。チームメンバーの独自の背景、視点、経験を重&lt;br&gt;視し、Waymo が事業を展開するコミュニティにさらに貢献できるよう、すべてのチームメンバーがアイデアを共有することをサポートし、奨励しています。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Waymo Operations exists to deliver the Waymo Driver to the world. We are a global team building and scaling the world&#39;s first and leading autonomous fleet and operations platform. From component sourcing to end customer management, we enable and create value for Waymo through scaled and orchestrated deployment of the Waymo Driver. At Waymo, we are dedicated to building a culture that promotes collaboration and celebration. We value our team members&#39; unique backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences and support and encourage all team members to share their ideas to help Waymo better serve the communities in which we operate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;業務内容: You Will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;戦略的リカバリ オペレーション: 路上での車両回収に向けた拡張可能な運用フレームワークの開発と実装を全工程にわたって推進し、複数の高密度市場でシームレスな牽引とロードサービスを確保します。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic Recovery Operations: Drive the end-to-end development and implementation of a scalable operational framework for on-road vehicle recovery, ensuring seamless towing and roadside support services across multiple high-density markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;ベンダー パフォーマンス管理: サードパーティの復旧パートナー（3PL）との関係を管理し、対応時間、安全認証、機器の準備状況に関する厳格なサービスレベル契約（SLA）を遵守させます。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vendor Performance Management: Manage relationships with third-party recovery partners (3PL), holding them to rigorous service-level agreements (SLAs) regarding response times, safety certifications, and equipment readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;インシデント対応と安全性: 複雑な復旧シナリオにおける主要なエスカレーション ポイントとして機能し、すべての現場作業が厳格な高電圧（HV）安全基準と自動運転システム プロトコルに準拠していることを確認します。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Incident Response &amp;amp; Safety: Act as the primary escalation point for complex recovery scenarios, ensuring all field maneuvers adhere to strict high-voltage (HV) safety standards and autonomous system protocols.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;運用スループットの推進: デポ オペレーションと連携して故障車両の到着とステージングを合理化し、「ラスト ワンマイル」の物流を最適化することで、ダウンタイムを最小限に抑え、整備士のスループットを最大化します。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive Operational Throughput: Optimize &quot;last-mile&quot; logistics by partnering with Depot Operations to streamline the arrival and staging of disabled vehicles, minimizing downtime and maximizing technician throughput.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;外部関係者との連携: 地域の法執行機関、初期対応者、自治体の運輸局（DOT）との連携を主導し、路上でのインシデント発生時における自動運転車の対応手順を標準化します。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;External Stakeholder Liaison: Lead coordination with local Law Enforcement, First Responders, and Municipal DOTs to standardize how autonomous vehicles are handled during roadside incidents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;分析とイノベーション: データ主導の分析情報を活用して、体系的な傾向とボトルネックを特定し、フリート全体の効率化と安全性の向上に役立つ、経営幹部向けのレポートを提供します。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze &amp;amp; Innovate: Use data-driven insights to identify systemic trends and bottlenecks, providing executive-ready reporting that informs fleet-wide efficiency and safety improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;必須条件: You Have:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;大規模な商用車フリートの運用、車両回収、またはリスクの高い物流を主導した 7 年以上の実務経験。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 7+ years of experience leading large-scale commercial fleet operations, vehicle recovery, or high-stakes logistics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;技術と安全重視: 高電圧シャットダウン手順や、大容量バッテリー搭載車の牽引に伴う複雑な対応など、電&amp;nbsp;気自動車のプラットフォームに関する 5 年以上の実務経験。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical &amp;amp; Safety Oriented: 5+ years of EV platforms experience, including high-voltage shutdown procedures and the complexities of towing heavy-battery vehicles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ベンダー管理の卓越性: 複雑な SLA を管理し、データ主導のパフォーマンス監査を通じてサードパーティの責任を推進した経験。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vendor Management Excellence: Experience managing complex SLAs and driving third-party accountability through data-driven performance audits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;複数市場の連携: 24 時間 365 日、高速で変化する環境下で、複数の地域にまたがる分散チームを率いた実&amp;nbsp;績。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multi-Market Coordination: Demonstrated ability to lead distributed teams across multiple geographies in a high-velocity, 24/7 environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;データ主導: 分析の厳密さを重視し、運用指標を活用して車両回収あたりのコスト削減や対応時間の最適化&amp;nbsp;を推進できること。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-Driven: You thrive on analytical rigor, using operational metrics to reduce the cost-per-recovery and optimize response times.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;関係者と規制当局との連携: 社内の部門横断型チーム、市当局、規制機関と連携して、運用目標を自治体の&amp;nbsp;要件と安全基準に適合させた実績。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder &amp;amp; Regulatory Engagement: Demonstrated success collaborating with internal cross-functional teams, city officials, and regulatory bodies to align operational goals with municipal requirements and safety standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;歓迎条件: We Prefer&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;経営幹部およびステークホルダーとのコミュニケーション: 口頭および書面での優れたコミュニケーション能力。複数の地理的市場にわたって、上級職員、自治体リーダー、戦略的パートナーと関わり、影響を与え&amp;nbsp;ることができる能力。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive &amp;amp; Stakeholder Communication: Strong verbal and written communication skills with a proven ability to engage and influence senior officials, municipal leaders, and strategic partners across multiple geographic markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;運用財務の洞察力: フリート インフラストラクチャの OpEx（運用費）予算の管理と費用対効果分析の実施&amp;nbsp;経験。特に「車両回収あたりの総費用」の最適化と長期的な資産投資収益率（ROI）に重点を置くこと。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operational Financial Acumen: Experience managing OpEx budgets and performing cost-benefit analyses for fleet infrastructure, with a focus on optimizing &quot;total cost per recovery&quot; and long-term asset ROI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;自動運転車（AV）業界の経験: 「ゴースト」ソフトウェア、手動オーバーライド ツール、キャリブレーショ&amp;nbsp;ンに影響を与えない安全な輸送など、自動運転車の復旧に関する実務経験。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AV Industry Experience: Direct experience with autonomous vehicle recovery, including the use of &quot;ghosting&quot; software, manual override tools, and calibration-safe transport.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;初期対応者トレーニング: 火災科学、緊急事態管理、または特殊な牽引（WreckMaster 認定など）のバック&amp;nbsp;グラウンド。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;First Responder Training: Background in fire science, emergency management, or specialized towing (e.g., WreckMaster certification).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;プロセス エンジニアリング: リーンまたはシックスシグマの原則を実装して、「路肩での停車時間」や運用&amp;nbsp;上の遅延を削減した経験。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process Engineering: Experience implementing Lean or Six Sigma principles to reduce &quot;roadside dwell time&quot; and operational drag.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;規制に関する経験: 自動運転車のテストや商用牽引に関する州レベルの DMV（車両管理局）および DOT（運&amp;nbsp;輸局）の規制に精通していること。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regulatory Experience: Familiarity with state-level DMV and DOT regulations regarding autonomous vehicle testing and commercial towing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Our vehicle engineers work with the cars of the future every day. We touch every part of the vehicle — electrical and thermal systems, chassis and interiors, power and energy storage and beyond — as we add self-driving power to existing auto designs and create new systems of our own. Our goal: To build a new generation of high-performing vehicles that are comfortable, reliable and safe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role follows a hybrid work schedule and you will report to a Lead Mechanical Simulation Engineer.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full Vehicle NVH Architecture: &lt;/strong&gt;Define and implement the complete vehicle NVH strategy, from top-level vehicle requirements to component-level targets, end-to-end engineering including tracking and delivery of targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design and Integration: &lt;/strong&gt;Lead the implementation of the NVH strategy for the integration of the Self Driving System and the base vehicle platform. Where necessary influencing all elements of the integration and vehicle/system design to ensure a quiet and calm environment for our end users, including: body structure, powertrain mounts, suspension, tires, acoustic treatments, isolations etc&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Simulation and Analysis:&lt;/strong&gt; Utilize advanced CAE tools (e.g., finite element analysis (FEA), statistical energy analysis (SEA)) to predict, analyze, and optimize NVH characteristics throughout the product development cycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Testing and Validation:&lt;/strong&gt; Plan, execute, and analyze vehicle and component-level NVH tests (e.g., sound quality, road noise, wind noise, powertrain contribution) both in the lab and on the road&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technology leadership and Problem Solving:&lt;/strong&gt; Stay current with and drive the adoption of emerging NVH technologies, materials, and measurement techniques, develop innovative solutions like utilizing cabin noise and induced sound through speakers to predict mechanical failures, lead root cause analysis and develop robust engineering countermeasures for complex NVH issues identified during virtual and physical validation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with Waymo internal design teams and OEM partners to ensure NVH solutions are compatible with all other vehicle attributes and develop detailed NVH models for the Waymo components in collaboration with the CAE team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master’s Degree in Mechanical Engineering with minimum 12 years of experience in automotive NVH engineering with increasing responsibility, including significant experience in full vehicle design/analysis and target setting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep theoretical and practical knowledge of acoustics, vibration, modal analysis, and sound quality metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in NVH CAE tools like Nastran, Optistruct and Abaqus, NVH signal processing tools, and familiarity in model building with tools like Hypermesh, Simlab and Ansa.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in NVH test equipment and software (e.g., B&amp;amp;K, Simcenter Testlab, VIacoustics) and expertise in performing NVH tests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with electric vehicle (EV) NVH challenges, including driveline whine, brake noise, and battery pack isolation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with global automotive NVH regulations and standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the selection and application of door seals, cabin interior trims, thermal ducts materials, and other acoustic materials for NVH&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The expected base salary range for this full-time position across US locations is listed below. Actual starting pay will be based on job-related factors, including exact work location, experience, relevant training and education, and skill level. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for the role location or, if the role can be performed remote, the specific salary range for your preferred location, during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Waymo employees are also eligible to participate in Waymo’s discretionary annual bonus program, equity incentive plan, and generous Company benefits program, subject to eligibility requirements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$230,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$284,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Waymo Safety team works to promote and help to continuously improve the safety of Waymo’s fully autonomous driving technology. Our experts develop safety goals and strategies, and conduct safety engineering analyses to ensure safety is being considered throughout the design and development of our vehicles. The team develops and promotes safety strategies and policies for autonomous vehicles for its work with regulatory authorities, lawmakers, law enforcement and public and non-profit organizations. Our Safety Team also helps advise on compliance with applicable environmental, health, and safety regulations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In this hybrid role you will report into our Program Manager, Resilience Policy &amp;amp; Process.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, own, and continuously improve resilience policies, standards, and plans (including incident and crisis response), ensuring direct alignment with Waymo&#39;s Safety Management System (SMS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cultivate and manage robust cross-functional partnerships (e.g., with Product, Engineering, Operations, Facilities, Legal, and Policy) to design complex process flows, escalation pathways, and robust operational tooling for event-response protocols globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead value stream and process mapping initiatives (from monitoring/triggers to severity categorization) and project manage sub-working groups to standardize resilient workflows across new and existing markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvement and SMS assurance by incorporating post-incident reviews and retrospectives to determine root causes, identify corrective actions, and prevent future occurrences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure vendor and partner continuity plans are robustly aligned to support scalability; support the organization&#39;s preparation for external audits, inspections, or regulatory assessments across new global geos.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience building and writing policy, standards, and processes, especially in resilience, incident management, operations, and/or business continuity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of strong cross-functional partnership with diverse stakeholders, especially to design complex process and escalation flows with a Product and Engineering focus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extreme curiosity to understand the status quo, always asks “why?”, and considers alternatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional attention to detail with the ability to synthesize complex information into clear and concise documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience reviewing and participating in after action reviews and retrospectives to identify action items for continuous improvement initiatives. Ability to productively solicit feedback and input from stakeholders to build a comprehensive narrative.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with technical writing, especially in a Safety, Product, or Operations focused environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in the autonomous, transportation, and/or weather forecast and response fields.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience contributing to the implementation or revision of Safety Management Systems (SMS) or equivalent compliance programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in highly regulated industries such as Automotive, Maritime, Aviation, or similar sectors, providing familiarity with safety-critical systems, compliance frameworks, and complex operational procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certifications or other relevant experience with incident management and business continuity best practices and frameworks (e.g., NIMS/ICS, ITIL Incident Management, or similar), indicating a structured approach to incident handling and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As required, &amp;lt; 20%&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
