&lt;li&gt;Provide senior-level legal support for sensitive internal investigations and compliance with local labor standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prevent and resolve employment disputes and proactively respond to regulatory agency claims, audits, and inquiries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide employment legal support for HR, Operations and other cross-functional teams in Western Europe as needed, including coordinating and overseeing local outside counsel across various European jurisdictions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At a minimum, we’d like you to have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Juris Doctor, LL.B., or equivalent law degree with a strong academic record&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience practicing employment law representing management at a law firm and/or in-house corporate setting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualified to practice law and in good standing in the UK (England and Wales)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive expertise in UK and European international employment laws and complex cross-border practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience navigating European labor relations, collective consultation processes, or engagement with works councils&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience advising HR, Operations and other cross-functional teams on managing contingent workforce needs within global operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication skills, with the ability to manage high-priority initiatives independently under deadline pressure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It’s preferred if you have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising fast-growing U.S.-headquartered technology companies with operations across the UK and continental Europe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct in-house corporate legal experience or a substantial secondment within a dynamic technology environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in complex, ambiguous environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
