&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Establish strategic technical partnerships with the simulation team to co-design well-defined and extensible APIs&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate, test, and validate the latest state of the art simulation technologies with our collision avoidance testing framework&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop new tools and capabilities to automate test quality and performance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor more junior engineers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS in Computer Science or a related field&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in Software Engineering&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to design robust, scalable, and maintainable software architectures and APIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong C++ and Python coding skills&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical leadership skills, with the ability to drive strategy, influence across teams, and mentor other engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master’s degree or PhD&amp;nbsp; in Computer Science or a related field&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in autonomous vehicles or robotics&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with simulation systems&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
