&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo&#39;s Systems Engineering team works together to blend software and hardware systems in groundbreaking new ways. We set the high performance standards that ensure our vehicles run smoothly and keep passengers safe, then design and perform the tests that validate that performance. We&#39;re looking for talented teammates who’ll help us maintain strong teamwork and are passionate about driving results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role follows a hybrid work schedule and reports to a Systems Test Engineering Manager, Structured Testing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Govern the operational performance and output of a large-scale test engineering program comprised of&amp;nbsp; Vendor Test Engineers working across multiple vendors and three proving grounds&amp;nbsp; and covering Systems Engineering technical domains including: Sensing, Perception, Motion Control, Fault Protection, Low Voltage, Cyber Security, Hardware in the Loop,&amp;nbsp; and Commercialization domains&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive towards alignment on strategic handover of technical&amp;nbsp; Engineering workflows and project responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Waymo technical leads to establish long term project roadmaps to ensure that the latest automation and AI tooling is being incorporated into the testing pipeline to ensure that our testing can provide comprehensive coverage while efficiently utilizing resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand how to develop sustainable and repeatable engineering workflows from unstructured one off development processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with engineering partners to create the ideal organizational structure and Engineering process flows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create a culture of Engineering excellence at scale for a growing Engineering organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in real world testing in automotive, aerospace or robotics, including test equipment, data acquisition, and automated analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience establishing new engagements with vendors providing engineering, testing, or operational services&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to effectively lead large cross functional teams and projects without direct authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience in successfully transitioning large engineering workflows from an established team to a new Engineering organization.&amp;nbsp; Examples include transitioning workflows&amp;nbsp; from an overseas OEM to a local team, or from a company’s HQ to a remote location&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing&amp;nbsp; a new Engineering organization and establishing&amp;nbsp; effective methodologies and processes to allow the team to take on new and specialized technical workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with automotive&amp;nbsp; testing across a diverse range of operating&amp;nbsp; conditions and technical domains. (Vehicle Dynamics, ADAS, Noise and Vibration, Durability, Sensing, Perception, etc.)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with physical hands-on testing of Autonomous Vehicles and related technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience converting manually executed and analyzed test campaigns into more efficient automated verification methodologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of Systems Engineering principles and experience with verification coverage plans developed from system level requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domestic and International Travel: 20%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The expected base salary range for this full-time position across US locations is listed below. Actual starting pay will be based on job-related factors, including exact work location, experience, relevant training and education, and skill level. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for the role location or, if the role can be performed remote, the specific salary range for your preferred location, during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Waymo employees are also eligible to participate in Waymo’s discretionary annual bonus program, equity incentive plan, and generous Company benefits program, subject to eligibility requirements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$230,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$284,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The Waymo Sustainability Team oversees the company’s environmental strategy and implementation. Our goal is to empower everyone to move sustainably by expanding access to shared electric vehicles and supporting more walkable, bikeable, and transit-rich communities. To achieve this, we advance sustainability programs that maximize environmental outcomes, conduct technoeconomic environmental analyses across our fleet, and work cross-functionally across the company to implement sustainable practices throughout our product and vehicle lifecycles. Additionally, our team designs environmental standards across the value chain and executes programs that support regulatory compliance, build alignment with key stakeholders, and earn trust in the communities we serve.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In this role, you will report to our Head of Sustainability &amp;amp; Environment.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive sustainability programs to meet international environmental standards and support sustainability policy goals accross a variety of functional areas of the value chain (clean energy, fleet, hardware, transit integration, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage environmental compliance against regulatory requirements, drive environmental mitigations, and quantify positive sustainability impacts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with internal teams (engineering, operations, product) to integrate sustainability into their work as well as engaging with external stakeholders (NGOs, government agencies, industry partners) on sustainability initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage international specific compliance, reporting, and verification requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate Waymo&#39;s sustainability efforts to internal and external audiences via presentations, reports, communications and marketing, comment letters and policy briefs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support GHG inventory and mitigation models to support international expansion and ensure environmental claims are audit-ready.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic expertise implementing environmental compliance and sustainability programs across a complex value chain within a highly regulated industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to synthesize complex environmental standards into actionable compliance roadmaps for international transportation ecosystems and large-scale fleet operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The vision to develop and execute comprehensive sustainability strategies that align with long-term corporate goals by defining clear targets, identifying key initiatives, and measuring ongoing progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management skills to lead sustainability initiatives from conception to completion across a variety of functional areas (clean energy, fleet, hardware, transit integration, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The technical acumen to draft the specific requirements and frameworks needed to quantify and measure Waymo’s environmental performance and net benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and interpersonal skills to seamlessly engage with diverse internal stakeholders (such as engineering and commercial teams) as well as external partners (including NGOs, government agencies, and industry peers).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong background in environmental management, compliance, and risk mitigation in a highly regulated industry.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broad experience developing and implementing clean energy, sustainability, and lifecycle management programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build, implement, document, and optimize reporting workflows for complex operational processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel up to 20-25% of the time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The expected base salary range for this full-time position is listed below. Actual starting pay will be based on job-related factors, including exact work location, experience, relevant training and education, and skill level.&amp;nbsp; Waymo employees are also eligible to participate in Waymo’s discretionary annual bonus program, equity incentive plan, and generous Company benefits program, subject to eligibility requirements. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;£88,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;£92,500 GBP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Waymo Operations exists to deliver the Waymo Driver to the world. We are a global team building and scaling the world&#39;s first and leading autonomous fleet and operations platform. From component sourcing to end customer management, we enable and create value for Waymo through scaled and orchestrated deployment of the Waymo Driver. At Waymo, we are dedicated to building a culture that promotes collaboration and celebration. We value our team members&#39; unique backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences and support and encourage all team members to share their ideas to help Waymo better serve the communities in which we operate.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;System Disruption Management, within the Global Operations Center, serves as the control point for disruptions across Waymo, orchestrating operations-driven cross-functional coordination to ensure rider safety, fleet resilience, and business performance remain uncompromised as we scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will report to the Head of System Disruption Management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead as the Incident Commander during cross-functional disruptions - orchestrating response efforts, making decisive real-time decisions, and coordinating all necessary stakeholders to safely and efficiently resolve events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and prioritize escalations - ensuring targeted stakeholder representation (e.g., Legal, Ops, Safety, Policy, &amp;amp; Communications) throughout the incident lifecycle.&lt;br&gt;Develop robust cross-functional partnerships - to proactively understand stakeholder concerns during events and effectively communicate post-incident outcomes and learning opportunities to a global audience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely within global Operations teams - providing critical support and guidance during real-time incident response to maintain seamless 24/7 coverage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvement - by leading thorough incident retrospectives to accurately document events and identify root causes. Define actionable follow-ups and track their implementation to continuously enhance safety, efficiency, and overall incident response capabilities for a distributed team, ensuring lessons learned are integrated back into processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver executive-level communications - on active incidents and present comprehensive analyses of key outcomes, trends, and strategic learnings from past events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of direct experience in incident management, having served as an Incident Commander or lead responder for high-severity, cross-functional incidents within a complex operational environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven technical expertise &amp;amp; cross-functional leadership, apply technical understanding of complex engineering systems to drive incident response, root cause analysis, and remediation for live operational incidents, coupled with an exceptional ability to build and align diverse stakeholders (e.g., Engineering, Legal, Operations) during critical events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated capability to remain calm and decisive under pressure, efficiently coordinating response efforts and making sound judgments in rapidly evolving, high-stakes situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience briefing senior executives and leadership, in real-time, on complex, fast-moving incidents, articulating technical details, impact, and proposed resolutions clearly and concisely across various communication channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional attention to detail with a track record of meticulously documenting incident timelines, contributing factors, and post-incident analysis to drive accurate reporting and continuous improvement.&lt;br&gt;Willingness and ability to participate in a 24/7 on-call rotation, demonstrating flexibility to cover shifts as part of a global &quot;follow the sun&quot; incident response capability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced degree in a relevant field such as Emergency Management, Business, Operations, Law, or a related discipline, demonstrating a deeper theoretical understanding of incident dynamics and organizational response.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading crisis and incident response as an Incident Commander in large-scale or high-impact environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to effectively interact with and/or report to external stakeholders, including law enforcement, regulatory agencies, and legal counsel, during sensitive or high-profile incidents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in highly regulated industries such as Automotive, Maritime, Aviation, or similar sectors, providing familiarity with safety-critical systems, compliance frameworks, and complex operational procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certifications/alignment on relevant incident management best practices and frameworks (e.g., NIMS/ICS, ITIL Incident Management, or similar), indicating a structured approach to incident handling and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with event mapping initiatives to enhance incident action planning, ensure congruence with response team actions, and promote stakeholder coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The expected base salary range for this full-time position across US locations is listed below. Actual starting pay will be based on job-related factors, including exact work location, experience, relevant training and education, and skill level. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for the role location or, if the role can be performed remote, the specific salary range for your preferred location, during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Waymo employees are also eligible to participate in Waymo’s discretionary annual bonus program, equity incentive plan, and generous Company benefits program, subject to eligibility requirements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$159,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$196,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo Operations は、Waymo Driver を世界に届けるための存在です。私たちは、世界初となる大型の自動運転フリートおよびオペレーション プラットフォームを構築し、スケーリングするグローバル チームです。部品調達からエンド カスタマーの管理まで、Waymo Driver を大規模かつ組織的に展開することで Waymo の価値を実現・創造します。Waymo は、協働と称賛を促す文化の構築に尽力しています。私たちはチームメンバーの独自の背景、視点、経験を尊重し、Waymo が事業を展開する地域社会にさらに貢献していけるよう、すべてのメンバーがアイデアを共有することをサポートし、奨励しています。&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;このポジションは、システム障害管理責任者の直属となります。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Waymo Operations exists to deliver the Waymo Driver to the world. We are a global team building and scaling the world&#39;s first and leading autonomous fleet and operations platform. From component sourcing to end customer management, we enable and create value for Waymo through scaled and orchestrated deployment of the Waymo Driver. At Waymo, we are dedicated to building a culture that promotes collaboration and celebration. We value our team members&#39; unique backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences and support and encourage all team members to share their ideas to help Waymo better serve the communities in which we operate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role you will report to the Head of System Disruption Management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;業務内容: You Will:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;部門横断的な障害発生時にインシデント コマンダーとして対応を主導する - 対応作業を指揮し、リアルタイムで重大な意思決定を行い、必要な関係者全員と連携して、イベントを安全かつ効率的に解決する。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead as the Incident Commander during cross-functional disruptions - orchestrating response efforts, making decisive real-time decisions, and coordinating all necessary stakeholders to safely and efficiently resolve events.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;エスカレーションを管理し、優先順位を付ける - インシデントのライフサイクル全体を通じて、対象となる関係者（法務、オペレーション、安全、ポリシー、コミュニケーションなど）の関与体制を確保する。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Manage and prioritize escalations - ensuring targeted stakeholder representation (e.g., Legal, Ops, Safety, Policy, &amp;amp; Communications) throughout the incident lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;部門を横断した強固なパートナーシップを構築する - イベント発生時には関係者の懸念事項を事前に把握し、インシデント後は結果と得られた知見を世界各地のオーディエンスに効果的に伝える。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Develop robust cross-functional partnerships - to proactively understand stakeholder concerns during events and effectively communicate post-incident outcomes and learning opportunities to a global audience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;グローバル オペレーション チームと緊密に連携する - リアルタイムのインシデント対応時に重要なサポートとガイダンスを提供して、24 時間 365 日のシームレスな対応体制を維持する。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate closely within global Operations teams - providing critical support and guidance during real-time incident response to maintain seamless 24/7 coverage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;継続的改善を推進する - 徹底的なインシデント事後分析を主導して、イベントを正確に文書化し、根本原因を特定する。実践的なフォローアップを定め、その実施状況を追跡することで、分散型チームの安全性、効率性、全体的なインシデント対応能力を継続的に強化しつつ、得られた知見をプロセスに組み込む。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drive continuous improvement - by leading thorough incident retrospectives to accurately document events and identify root causes. Define actionable follow-ups and track their implementation to continuously enhance safety, efficiency, and overall incident response capabilities for a distributed team, ensuring lessons learned are integrated back into processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;経営幹部レベルのコミュニケーション - 発生中のインシデントについて報告し、過去のイベントの主な結果、傾向、戦略的知見の包括的な分析を提示する。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deliver executive-level communications - on active incidents and present comprehensive analyses of key outcomes, trends, and strategic learnings from past events.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;必須条件: You Have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;複雑な運用環境において、重大度の高い部門横断的なインシデントのインシデント コマンダーまたはリード レスポンダーを務めた、インシデント管理における 5 年以上の実務経験。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;5+ years of direct experience in incident management, having served as an Incident Commander or lead responder for high-severity, cross-functional incidents within a complex operational environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;実績に裏打ちされた技術的専門知識と部門横断的なリーダーシップ。複雑なエンジニアリング システムに関する技術的理解を応用して、発生中の運用インシデントに対するインシデント対応、根本原因分析、是正を推進するとともに、重大イベントの際にさまざまなステークホルダー（エンジニアリング、法務、オペレーションなど）との関係を構築し、連携させる優れた能力を持つこと。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Proven technical expertise &amp;amp; cross-functional leadership, apply technical understanding of complex engineering systems to drive incident response, root cause analysis, and remediation for live operational incidents, coupled with an exceptional ability to build and align diverse stakeholders (e.g., Engineering, Legal, Operations) during critical events.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;プレッシャーの中でも冷静かつ果断に行動し、迅速に変化するリスクの高い状況下で、対応作業を効率的に調整し、適切な判断を下す能力。• 複雑で急速に変化するインシデントについて、さまざまなコミュニケーション チャネルを通じて、技術的な詳細、影響、提案された解決策を上級幹部やリーダーにリアルタイムで明確かつ簡潔に報告した経験。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Demonstrated capability to remain calm and decisive under pressure, efficiently coordinating response efforts and making sound judgments in rapidly evolving, high-stakes situations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;細部への高い注意力を備え、インシデントのタイムライン、要因、事後分析を綿密に文書化し、正確な報告と継続的改善を推進してきた実績があること。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience briefing senior executives and leadership, in real-time, on complex, fast-moving incidents, articulating technical details, impact, and proposed resolutions clearly and concisely across various communication channels.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;24 時間 365 日のオンコール ローテーションに加わる意欲と能力があり、グローバルな「フォローザサン」形態のインシデント対応体制の一員としてシフトを柔軟にカバーできること。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Willingness and ability to participate in a 24/7 on-call rotation, demonstrating flexibility to cover shifts as part of a global &quot;follow the sun&quot; incident response capability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;歓迎条件: We Prefer:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;緊急事態管理、ビジネス、オペレーション、法律、または関連分野の高度な学位を取得しており、インシデントのダイナミクスと組織の対応に関する理論的な理解の深さを示せること。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Advanced degree in a relevant field such as Emergency Management, Business, Operations, Law, or a related discipline, demonstrating a deeper theoretical understanding of incident dynamics and organizational response.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;大規模または影響の大きい環境で、インシデント コマンダーとして危機対応とインシデント対応を主導した経験。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience leading crisis and incident response as an Incident Commander in large-scale or high-impact environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;センシティブなインシデントや注目度の高いインシデントが発生した際に、法執行機関、規制機関、弁護士などの外部関係者と効果的にやり取りや報告を行った実績。• 自動車、海運、航空などの規制の厳しい業界または同様の分野での経験があり、安全上重要なシステム、コンプライアンス フレームワーク、複雑な運用手順に精通していること。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to effectively interact with and/or report to external stakeholders, including law enforcement, regulatory agencies, and legal counsel, during sensitive or high-profile incidents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;関連するインシデント管理のベスト プラクティスとフレームワーク（NIMS / ICS、ITIL インシデント管理など）に関する認定資格や準拠した知識を持ち、インシデント処理と継続的改善に対する構造化されたアプローチを示せること。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience in highly regulated industries such as Automotive, Maritime, Aviation, or similar sectors, providing familiarity with safety-critical systems, compliance frameworks, and complex operational procedures.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;インシデント対応計画の強化、対応チームの行動との整合性の確保、関係者の連携の促進を目的としたイベント マッピング イニシアチブの経験。&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Certifications/alignment on relevant incident management best practices and frameworks (e.g., NIMS/ICS, ITIL Incident Management, or similar), indicating a structured approach to incident handling and continuous improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Waymo Safety team works to promote and help to continuously improve the safety of Waymo&#39;s fully autonomous driving technology. Our experts develop safety goals and strategies, and conduct safety engineering analyses to ensure safety is being considered throughout the design and development of our vehicles. The team develops and promotes safety strategies and policies for autonomous vehicles for its work with regulatory authorities, lawmakers, law enforcement and public and non-profit organizations. Our Safety Team also helps advise on compliance with applicable environmental, health, and safety regulations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In this hybrid role, you will report into one of our System Safety Leads.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional efforts to perform safety analyses and identify potential hazard and their causes, assess safety risks (qualitatively and quantitatively), support the definition of safety requirements, inform design decisions, propose mitigations, and support verification strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in hardware, software, and operations design and readiness reviews and discussions to help ensure that safety mitigations and requirements are addressed and ensure the safety mitigations are working effectively in the field&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide guidance on the adoption and adaptation of relevant safety standards, and industry best practices, and help ensure Waymo and its partners comply with relevant safety regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluates the continued effectiveness of implemented risk control strategies; supports the identification of new hazards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide leadership in defining, implementing, and improving relevant System Safety processes while promoting our safety culture inside Waymo&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide leadership in integrating the System Safety Methodology with other methodologies of the Waymo safety framewor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor of Science in Electrical/Mechatronics/Aerospace Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, or related technical fields&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical project management skills with the ability to manage multiple parallel projects&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of relevant engineering work experience that includes minimum 5 years of System Safety engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in selecting and performing appropriate inductive/deductive safety analyses in order to efficiently identify hazards and their level of risk&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in applying Systems Engineering principles&amp;nbsp; including defining SMART safety mitigations/requirements and collaborating on effective verification and validation methods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive background in risk management and aligning risk based decisions with stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Master’s degree or PhD in Electrical/Mechatronics/Aerospace Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, or related technical fields&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in complex, safety critical fleet operations and the impact to hardware, software, and systems design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel approximately 5% of the time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In accordance with Washington state law, we are highlighting our comprehensive benefits package, which is available to all eligible US based employees. Benefits for this role include:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Health, dental, vision, life, disability insurance&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Retirement Benefits: 401(k) with company match&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Paid Time Off: 20 days of vacation per year, accruing at a rate of 6.15 hours per pay period for the first five years of employment&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sick Time: 40 hours/year (statutory, where applicable); 5 days/event (discretionary)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Maternity Leave (Short-Term Disability + Baby Bonding): 28-30 weeks&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Baby Bonding Leave: 18 weeks&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Holidays: 13 paid days per year&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The expected base salary range for this full-time position across US locations is listed below. Actual starting pay will be based on job-related factors, including exact work location, experience, relevant training and education, and skill level. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for the role location or, if the role can be performed remote, the specific salary range for your preferred location, during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Waymo employees are also eligible to participate in Waymo’s discretionary annual bonus program, equity incentive plan, and generous Company benefits program, subject to eligibility requirements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$196,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$248,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Waymo&#39;s Systems Engineering team works together to blend software and hardware systems in groundbreaking new ways. We set the high performance standards that ensure our vehicles run smoothly and keep passengers safe, then design and perform the tests that validate that performance. We&#39;re looking for talented teammates who’ll help us maintain strong teamwork and are passionate about driving results.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role follows a hybrid work schedule and you will report to Systems Engineering Leadership.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional strategies to accelerate development for new product initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate new, complex use cases into actionable system requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute trade studies and investigation to influence cross-functional priorities and product roadmaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Systems Engineering and Test teams to develop and execute robust verification strategies that demonstrate critical requirements are met&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Innovate solutions for technical challenges within integrated hardware and software autonomous systems, covering the full day-in-the-life&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define concept of operations for new product initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s Degree in relevant Engineering or related field (including ME, EE, CS, Robotics, Controls, Aerospace, etc.) or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10 or more years of engineering experience with demonstrated delivery of hardware / software integrated vehicle or robotic systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience across full product lifecycle, from concept or pilot through transition into operations in a fast paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong foundation in systems engineering fundamentals such as requirements definition, formal verification and validation methods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data analysis and related script development skills (e.g. using Python, SQL, etc)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-functional technical leadership and mentorship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Degree in relevant Engineering or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience testing and deploying production-level safety critical systems, especially at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience influencing product strategy and user flows through iterative launches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Although not the focus of this role, some software development experience and understanding of SW development process is helpful&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Autonomous vehicle industry experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The expected base salary range for this full-time position across US locations is listed below. Actual starting pay will be based on job-related factors, including exact work location, experience, relevant training and education, and skill level. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for the role location or, if the role can be performed remote, the specific salary range for your preferred location, during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Waymo employees are also eligible to participate in Waymo’s discretionary annual bonus program, equity incentive plan, and generous Company benefits program, subject to eligibility requirements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$272,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$336,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo&#39;s Systems Engineering team works together to blend software and hardware systems in groundbreaking new ways. We set the high performance standards that ensure our vehicles run smoothly and keep passengers safe, then design and perform the tests that validate that performance. We&#39;re looking for talented teammates who&#39;ll help us maintain strong teamwork and are passionate about driving results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role follows a hybrid work schedule and you will report to a Staff Systems Engineer.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use your knowledge of perception systems combined with Waymo’s safety and business targets to propose requirements based on statistical, risk based arguments.&lt;/li&gt;
